&lt;em&gt;LPE2, LPF2, and LPH2 line-laser camera families.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;my-role&#34;&gt;My role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My work focuses on the line-laser algorithm pipeline: stripe/profile extraction, HDR fusion, vibration correction, stray-light suppression, point-cloud post-processing, geometric measurement, and Smart3 workflow deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;principle&#34;&gt;Principle&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The system follows laser triangulation. A cylindrical lens spreads the laser into a line on the target surface; reflected light is imaged by CMOS; the displacement and shape of the stripe are converted into profile height. The camera then outputs depth, point cloud, and intensity data for downstream measurement.&lt;/p&gt;
